{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EGL91j2gnzU9egVKqWBhpn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '核心detection优势不成立，需要完全reframe。推荐方向(1)方法论贡献型——将TF-IDF=1.0发现本身及register-normalization\n2\t  protocol作为核心贡献，论证现有multi-turn detection工作系统性高估检测能力。Paper type从\"new method\" 转向\"analysis/evaluation\n3\t  methodology\"，仍冲EMNLP main但投methodology track。\n4\t\n5\t  '\n6\timagined_experiments:\n7\t- name: data_quality_fix\n8\t  plan_id: plan_001\n9\t  description: Register-normalize jailbreak data + fix strategy=7 labeling,验证TF-IDF降到<0.75\n10\t  expected_results:\n11\t    tfidf_before_normalization: 1.0\n12\t    tfidf_after_first_pass: 0.82\n13\t    tfidf_after_second_pass: 0.73\n14\t    normalization_rounds_needed: 2\n15\t    label_fix_applied: true\n16\t    benign_strategy_class: none_class_9\n17\t  result_rationale: 'TF-IDF需要两轮normalization才降到阈值以下（0.73），说明原始数据中jailbreak和benign的register差异\n18\t    极大——攻击对话使用了明显不同于benign的词汇分布（更formal/technical的register、特定prompt模板词汇）。 第一轮paraphrase仅消除表层模板词但保留了domain-specific术语差异，需要第二轮targeted\n19\t    normalization 才勉强达标。这本身就是一个强信号：原始pilot phase_b的perfect F1=1.0主要来自lexical shortcut。\n20\t\n21\t    '\n22\t  tables:\n23\t  - caption: TF-IDF Separation After Each Normalization Round\n24\t    rows:\n25\t    - - raw_data\n26\t      - 1.0\n27\t      - Perfect lexical separation\n28\t    - - round_1_paraphrase\n29\t      - 0.82\n30\t      - Template words removed, register gap remains\n31\t    - - round_2_targeted\n32\t      - 0.73\n33\t      - Barely passes gate after domain term normalization\n34\t  figures_description:\n35\t  - 'TF-IDF feature importance heatmap showing top-50 discriminative tokens before/after\n36\t    normalization — before: dominated by prompt template tokens and register markers;\n37\t    after: residual separation from topic words not fully removable without destroying\n38\t    content'\n39\t  analysis: 'HARD GATE通过但仅勉强（0.73 vs 阈值0.75）。两轮normalization的必要性本身是方法论贡献的核心evidence：\n40\t    它证明multi-turn jailbreak detection benchmark中存在系统性lexical confound。在reframe方向(1)下，\n41\t    这个实验的finding从\"obstacle to overcome\"变为\"primary contribution\"。\n42\t\n43\t    '\n44\t- name: core_revalidation_clean\n45\t  plan_id: plan_002\n46\t  description: 在clean data上重新训练treatment和baseline，全K值评估\n47\t  expected_results:\n48\t    treatment_k1_f1_clean: 0.68\n49\t    baseline_k1_f1_clean: 0.66\n50\t    treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.72\n51\t    baseline_k2_f1_clean: 0.7\n52\t    treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.78\n53\t    baseline_k3_f1_clean: 0.76\n54\t    treatment_k5_f1_clean: 0.83\n55\t    baseline_k5_f1_clean: 0.82\n56\t    treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.86\n57\t    baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.85\n58\t    delta_k2_pp: 2\n59\t    delta_k3_pp: 2\n60\t    delta_full_pp: 1\n61\t    deberta_persuasion_acc_clean: 0.63\n62\t  result_rationale: '去除lexical confound后，treatment与baseline的差距从原始的10+pp收缩到1-2pp（不显著）。\n63\t    核心原因：DeBERTa persuasion分类器在clean data上accuracy从0.7963降到0.63——8-class taxonomy\n64\t    过于fine-grained，在register-normalized data上许多strategy boundary变得模糊（e.g., \"authority\n65\t    appeal\" vs \"logical appeal\"在paraphrase后难以区分）。由于persuasion encoder本身quality下降，其生成的\n66\t    embeddings不再携带比vanilla DeBERTa显著更多的信息。Baseline的vanilla DeBERTa embeddings在clean\n67\t    data上反而更稳定，因为它不依赖于noisy strategy labels。2pp的delta在72-sample test set上 bootstrap\n68\t    CI完全overlap，p>0.3。\n69\t\n70\t    '\n71\t  tables:\n72\t  - caption: 'F1 Comparison: Treatment vs Baseline on Clean Data (N=72 test)'\n73\t    rows:\n74\t    - - K=1\n75\t      - 0.68\n76\t      - 0.66\n77\t      - +2pp\n78\t      - p=0.41\n79\t    - - K=2\n80\t      - 0.72\n81\t      - 0.7\n82\t      - +2pp\n83\t      - p=0.35\n84\t    - - K=3\n85\t      - 0.78\n86\t      - 0.76\n87\t      - +2pp\n88\t      - p=0.32\n89\t    - - K=5\n90\t      - 0.83\n91\t      - 0.82\n92\t      - +1pp\n93\t      - p=0.58\n94\t    - - Full\n95\t      - 0.86\n96\t      - 0.85\n97\t      - +1pp\n98\t      - p=0.62\n99\t  - caption: 'DeBERTa Encoder Quality: Original vs Clean Data'\n100\t    rows:\n101\t    - - persuasion_acc_original\n102\t      - 0.7963\n103\t    - - persuasion_acc_clean\n104\t      - 0.63\n105\t    - - intent_acc_original\n106\t      - 0.9514\n107\t    - - intent_acc_clean\n108\t      - 0.88\n109\t  figures_description:\n110\t  - Paired bootstrap confidence interval plot for delta(treatment-baseline) at each\n111\t    K — all CIs cross zero\n112\t  - Confusion matrix for 8-class persuasion classifier on clean data showing heavy\n113\t    off-diagonal mass between adjacent strategies\n114\t  analysis: 'PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta_k2=2pp < required 5pp，且统计不显著。Persuasion grounding在去除\n115\t    lexical shortcut后不提供有意义增量。DeBERTa学到的主要是intent分类信号（acc仍0.88）而非persuasion strategy信号（acc降至0.63）。这意味着Claim\n116\t    2（early detection via persuasion grounding）在当前 数据/taxonomy下不成立。但这个negative result本身有价值：它说明仅fine-tune\n117\t    on persuasion labels 不足以在clean setting下获得detection优势，可能需要更大规模的persuasion标注数据或更粗粒度的taxonomy。\n118\t\n119\t    '\n120\t- name: scrambled_label_ablation\n121\t  plan_id: plan_003\n122\t  description: 随机打乱persuasion strategy labels重新训练，对比properly-labeled treatment\n123\t  expected_results:\n124\t    treatment_proper_k2_f1: 0.72\n125\t    treatment_scrambled_k2_f1: 0.7\n126\t    treatment_proper_full_f1: 0.86\n127\t    treatment_scrambled_full_f1: 0.84\n128\t    scrambled_label_drop_k2_pp: 2\n129\t    scrambled_label_drop_full_pp: 2\n130\t  result_rationale: 'Scrambled labels仅导致2pp下降（<4pp阈值），说明persuasion labels本身不是关键信号源。\n131\t    原因：在clean data上DeBERTa persuasion分类器本身就只有0.63 accuracy，意味着encoder学到的 representation中persuasion\n132\t    strategy信息就不强。Scrambled labels让encoder无法学到coherent strategy patterns，但由于原始labels在clean\n133\t    data上本就noisy（8类之间boundary模糊）， scrambling的marginal damage有限。真正驱动detection的是GRU从conversation-level\n134\t    temporal patterns中学到的信号（turn数、response长度变化等meta-features），这些不依赖于strategy labels\n135\t    的correctness。\n136\t\n137\t    '\n138\t  tables:\n139\t  - caption: Scrambled Label Ablation Results\n140\t    rows:\n141\t    - - K=2\n142\t      - 0.72\n143\t      - 0.7\n144\t      - -2pp\n145\t    - - K=3\n146\t      - 0.78\n147\t      - 0.76\n148\t      - -2pp\n149\t    - - Full\n150\t      - 0.86\n151\t      - 0.84\n152\t      - -2pp\n153\t  figures_description:\n154\t  - 'Bar chart: proper vs scrambled label performance across K values — gaps uniformly\n155\t    small and within CI'\n156\t  analysis: '结论：persuasion strategy labels在clean data regime下不carry significant signal\n157\t    beyond acting as a noisy regularizer。这支持worst-tier核心假设——当前taxonomy粒度（8 classes）在480-sample\n158\t    regime下无法学到robust strategy representations。对reframe方向的implication：不能claim \"persuasion\n159\t    labels are the key ingredient\"，但可以claim \"current taxonomy granularity is insufficient\"作为future\n160\t    work direction。\n161\t\n162\t    '\n163\t- name: adversarial_perturbation\n164\t  plan_id: plan_004\n165\t  description: 对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing，评估treatment\n166\t    vs baseline degradation\n167\t  expected_results:\n168\t    treatment_f1_before_perturbation: 0.86\n169\t    treatment_f1_after_perturbation: 0.71\n170\t    baseline_f1_before_perturbation: 0.85\n171\t    baseline_f1_after_perturbation: 0.72\n172\t    treatment_drop_pp: 15\n173\t    baseline_drop_pp: 13\n174\t    delta_delta_pp: -2\n175\t    tfidf_f1_after_perturbation: 0.58\n176\t    tfidf_drop_pp: 15\n177\t  result_rationale: 'Treatment和baseline在perturbation下同步下降约14-15pp，delta-delta为-2pp（不显著且方向错误）。\n178\t    核心原因：adversarial paraphrasing不仅消除lexical cues（TF-IDF baseline崩溃到0.58），也破坏了 DeBERTa\n179\t    encoder（无论persuasion-grounded还是vanilla）所依赖的surface-level linguistic patterns。\n180\t    Persuasion-grounded encoder理论上应capture deeper pragmatic structure，但由于其persuasion\n181\t    classification本身就在clean data上只有0.63 accuracy，它学到的representation并不比vanilla encoder\n182\t    更\"pragmatic\"——两者都主要依赖sentence-level semantic features而非genuine illocutionary act\n183\t    encoding。Aggressive paraphrasing保留了propositional content但改变了sentence structure，\n184\t    两种encoder的degradation profile因此相似。\n185\t\n186\t    '\n187\t  tables:\n188\t  - caption: Adversarial Perturbation Results (Full Conversation)\n189\t    rows:\n190\t    - - Treatment\n191\t      - 0.86\n192\t      - 0.71\n193\t      - -15pp\n194\t    - - Baseline\n195\t      - 0.85\n196\t      - 0.72\n197\t      - -13pp\n198\t    - - TF-IDF+LR\n199\t      - 0.73\n200\t      - 0.58\n201\t      - -15pp\n202\t  - caption: Delta-Delta Analysis\n203\t    rows:\n204\t    - - treatment_drop\n205\t      - -15\n206\t    - - baseline_drop\n207\t      - -13\n208\t    - - delta_delta\n209\t      - -2\n210\t      - wrong direction, n.s.\n211\t  figures_description:\n212\t  - Degradation waterfall chart showing parallel decline for treatment and baseline\n213\t    under perturbation levels (light/moderate/aggressive)\n214\t  - 'Scatter plot: per-conversation F1 change under perturbation, treatment vs baseline\n215\t    — points clustered around diagonal (no systematic advantage)'\n216\t  analysis: 'PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta-delta=-2pp，方向错误且不显著（需要>3pp正向）。Claim 1（Pragmatic\n217\t    Evasion Asymmetry）在empirical层面不成立——persuasion-grounded features并不比semantic features\n218\t    更robust to perturbation。这是worst tier最致命的finding：理论上最elegant的claim（pragmatic patterns\n219\t    structurally harder to evade）没有empirical support。TF-IDF baseline的崩溃（-15pp） 确认perturbation有效消除了lexical\n220\t    cues，但treatment未能展现预期的robustness优势。\n221\t\n222\t    '\n223\t- name: multi_attack_generation\n224\t  plan_id: plan_005\n225\t  description: 生成FITD和Deceptive Delight两种额外攻击类型的对话数据\n226\t  expected_results:\n227\t    fitd_conversations_generated: 65\n228\t    deceptive_delight_conversations_generated: 58\n229\t    fitd_avg_turns: 6.2\n230\t    dd_avg_turns: 4.8\n231\t    fitd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 0.92\n232\t    dd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 0.89\n233\t    generation_quality_pass_rate: 0.78\n234\t  result_rationale: '数据生成本身不受tier影响——这是pipeline execution而非hypothesis testing。Qwen3-8B成功生成\n235\t    足够数量的对话，strategy annotation coverage >85%。但generation_quality_pass_rate（0.78）\n236\t    略低于ideal，部分生成的对话persuasion structure不够naturalistic（特别是Deceptive Delight 的interleaving\n237\t    pattern对LLM来说较难faithful reproduce）。这些数据将在plan_006的cross-attack evaluation中暴露问题。\n238\t\n239\t    '\n240\t  tables:\n241\t  - caption: Generated Attack Data Summary\n242\t    rows:\n243\t    - - FITD\n244\t      - 65\n245\t      - 6.2\n246\t      - 0.92\n247\t      - 0.81\n248\t    - - Deceptive_Delight\n249\t      - 58\n250\t      - 4.8\n251\t      - 0.89\n252\t      - 0.74\n253\t  figures_description:\n254\t  - Strategy distribution comparison across three attack types (Crescendo vs FITD\n255\t    vs Deceptive Delight) — shows different strategy emphasis patterns\n256\t  analysis: '数据生成成功满足pass criteria（>=50 per type）。但在worst tier context下，这些数据的价值 从\"generalization\n257\t    evidence for our method\"变为\"additional test cases revealing method limitations\"\n258\t    或\"attack diversity evidence for methodology paper\"。\n259\t\n260\t    '\n261\t- name: cross_attack_evaluation\n262\t  plan_id: plan_006\n263\t  description: 在FITD和Deceptive Delight上zero-shot评估Crescendo-trained模型\n264\t  expected_results:\n265\t    treatment_fitd_f1: 0.58\n266\t    baseline_fitd_f1: 0.56\n267\t    treatment_dd_f1: 0.54\n268\t    baseline_dd_f1: 0.52\n269\t    cross_attack_treatment_f1_avg: 0.56\n270\t    cross_attack_baseline_f1_avg: 0.54\n271\t    cross_attack_delta_pp: 2\n272\t  result_rationale: '两者都在unseen attack types上大幅下降（从0.85-0.86降到0.54-0.58），且treatment对baseline的\n273\t    优势仅2pp（不显著）。根本原因：如果persuasion grounding真的capture了attack-agnostic的pragmatic escalation\n274\t    pattern，treatment应在cross-attack setting下展现更强泛化能力（因为不同attack types 共享底层persuasion\n275\t    playbook）。但由于encoder学到的主要是Crescendo-specific的surface patterns 而非genuine pragmatic\n276\t    structure，cross-attack泛化能力与vanilla baseline无异。两者的low absolute performance（0.54-0.58）说明Crescendo-specific\n277\t    training signal（无论lexical还是semantic） 都不transfer well，这在worst tier下是预期内的——没有genuine\n278\t    pragmatic feature的robustness 保证，模型就是在overfit to training distribution。\n279\t\n280\t    '\n281\t  tables:\n282\t  - caption: Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Evaluation\n283\t    rows:\n284\t    - - FITD\n285\t      - 0.58\n286\t      - 0.56\n287\t      - +2pp\n288\t      - n.s.\n289\t    - - Deceptive_Delight\n290\t      - 0.54\n291\t      - 0.52\n292\t      - +2pp\n293\t      - n.s.\n294\t    - - Average\n295\t      - 0.56\n296\t      - 0.54\n297\t      - +2pp\n298\t      - n.s.\n299\t  figures_description:\n300\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: in-domain (Crescendo) vs cross-attack (FITD, DD) performance\n301\t    for treatment and baseline — both collapse similarly on OOD data'\n302\t  analysis: 'PASS CRITERIA FAILS。但对reframe方向(1)有正面意义：cross-attack failure + in-domain\n303\t    dependence on lexical cues共同论证了\"现有multi-turn detection方法泛化能力被高估\"的thesis。可作为 methodology\n304\t    paper中illustrating the problem的evidence。\n305\t\n306\t    '\n307\t- name: tfidf_lr_baseline\n308\t  plan_id: plan_007\n309\t  description: Clean data上的TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline\n310\t  expected_results:\n311\t    clean_tfidf_lr_f1: 0.7\n312\t    clean_tfidf_lr_precision: 0.72\n313\t    clean_tfidf_lr_recall: 0.68\n314\t    tfidf_feature_count_above_threshold: 47\n315\t  result_rationale: '即使在register-normalized data上（TF-IDF separation从1.0降到0.73），TF-IDF+LR仍能达到\n316\t    F1=0.70。这说明两轮normalization虽然消除了most obvious的register markers，但仍有residual lexical\n317\t    signal（47个features仍有discriminative power）。这意味着即使我们的\"clean data\" 仍然不完全clean——topic-level词汇差异（jailbreak\n318\t    conversations inevitably discuss different topics than benign ones）是无法完全消除的confound\n319\t    without destroying content validity。 这是methodology paper的核心argument之一：lexical\n320\t    confound在multi-turn detection中是 structural的，不仅仅是data hygiene问题。\n321\t\n322\t    '\n323\t  tables:\n324\t  - caption: TF-IDF+LR on Clean Data\n325\t    rows:\n326\t    - - F1\n327\t      - 0.7\n328\t    - - Precision\n329\t      - 0.72\n330\t    - - Recall\n331\t      - 0.68\n332\t    - - Discriminative_features\n333\t      - 47\n334\t  figures_description:\n335\t  - Top-20 TF-IDF features after normalization with weights — showing residual topic-level\n336\t    rather than register-level discrimination\n337\t  analysis: 'TF-IDF+LR的0.70 F1与neural models（treatment 0.86, baseline 0.85）之间的gap说明neural\n338\t    models 确实学到了beyond-lexical的signal。但treatment vs baseline的1pp gap说明这个beyond-lexical\n339\t    signal 不是来自persuasion grounding，而是来自generic sentence semantics。对evasion hierarchy\n340\t    narrative 的implication：lexical(0.70) < semantic(0.85) ≈ pragmatic(0.86)——hierarchy的后两层collapse了。\n341\t\n342\t    '\n343\t- name: strategy_transition_analysis\n344\t  plan_id: plan_008\n345\t  description: 计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy transition matrices并可视化\n346\t  expected_results:\n347\t    jailbreak_monotonicity_score: 0.52\n348\t    benign_monotonicity_score: 0.45\n349\t    monotonicity_gap: 0.07\n350\t    transition_entropy_jailbreak: 2.1\n351\t    transition_entropy_benign: 2.3\n352\t    clear_escalation_visible: false\n353\t  result_rationale: 'Jailbreak对话的monotonicity score（0.52）仅略高于benign（0.45），差距不足以支撑\"monotonic\n354\t    escalation trajectory\"的claim。原因有二：(1) DeBERTa persuasion classifier在clean data上\n355\t    accuracy=0.63意味着strategy labels本身就noisy，computed transitions基于noisy labels自然 pattern不清晰；(2)\n356\t    Register normalization改变了句子的surface form，部分breaks了persuasion classifier学到的pattern（它在original\n357\t    register上train的），导致strategy assignment在 normalized data上更random。Transition entropy差异也很小（2.1\n358\t    vs 2.3），说明jailbreak对话 并没有显著更deterministic的strategy progression。\n359\t\n360\t    '\n361\t  tables:\n362\t  - caption: 'Trajectory Statistics: Jailbreak vs Benign'\n363\t    rows:\n364\t    - - monotonicity_score\n365\t      - 0.52\n366\t      - 0.45\n367\t      - Δ=0.07\n368\t    - - transition_entropy\n369\t      - 2.1\n370\t      - 2.3\n371\t      - Δ=0.2\n372\t    - - dominant_path_frequency\n373\t      - 0.18\n374\t      - 0.14\n375\t      - Δ=0.04\n376\t  figures_description:\n377\t  - Strategy transition heatmap (jailbreak) — diffuse pattern without clear dominant\n378\t    path, most cells have non-trivial probability mass\n379\t  - Strategy transition heatmap (benign) — similar diffuse pattern, not clearly more\n380\t    'oscillatory' than jailbreak\n381\t  - 2D PCA trajectory plot — jailbreak and benign trajectories heavily overlap, no\n382\t    clear separation in strategy space\n383\t  analysis: 'Claim 3（Monotonic Escalation Trajectory）在clean data + noisy classifier\n384\t    regime下不成立。 这排除了reframe方向(2)（分析贡献型依赖trajectory可视化成立）。剩余可行方向：(1)方法论贡献型 或(3)negative\n385\t    result型。如果figures经过careful curation能找到个别illustrative examples showing escalation\n386\t    pattern，可以作为qualitative observation保留，但不能作为quantitative claim。\n387\t\n388\t    '\n389\t- name: wildchat_hard_negatives\n390\t  plan_id: plan_009\n391\t  description: 从WildChat筛选high-drift benign对话作为hard negatives评估FPR\n392\t  expected_results:\n393\t    wildchat_filtered_conversations: 120\n394\t    contamination_rate_before_filter: 0.15\n395\t    contamination_rate_after_filter: 0.03\n396\t    treatment_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.22\n397\t    baseline_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.2\n398\t    treatment_fpr_easy_negatives: 0.08\n399\t    baseline_fpr_easy_negatives: 0.09\n400\t  result_rationale: 'Treatment在hard negatives上的FPR（0.22）与baseline（0.20）相当，且都超过15%阈值。\n401\t    High-drift benign对话（e.g., 从casual聊天转向technical discussion的对话）会触发false positives，因为模型（无论treatment还是baseline）将conversation-level\n402\t    semantic drift 误判为adversarial escalation。Persuasion grounding理论上应区分\"genuine topic\n403\t    drift\" 和\"adversarial strategy escalation\"，但由于classifier accuracy不足（0.63），这种区分\n404\t    能力没有materialized。FPR=0.22在实际deployment中unacceptable。\n405\t\n406\t    '\n407\t  tables:\n408\t  - caption: False Positive Rate on WildChat Hard Negatives\n409\t    rows:\n410\t    - - Treatment_hard\n411\t      - 0.22\n412\t      - FAILS <15% threshold\n413\t    - - Baseline_hard\n414\t      - 0.2\n415\t      - FAILS <15% threshold\n416\t    - - Treatment_easy\n417\t      - 0.08\n418\t      - passes\n419\t    - - Baseline_easy\n420\t      - 0.09\n421\t      - passes\n422\t  figures_description:\n423\t  - FPR distribution across conversation drift levels — monotonically increasing for\n424\t    both models, treatment offers no advantage in high-drift regime\n425\t  analysis: 'PASS CRITERIA FAILS（FPR=0.22 > 15%阈值）。在reframe context下，这进一步支持\"current\n426\t    approaches conflate conversational drift with adversarial escalation\"的methodology\n427\t    critique。\n428\t\n429\t    '\n430\t- name: cross_checkpoint_variance\n431\t  plan_id: plan_010\n432\t  description: 评估多个DeBERTa fine-tuning checkpoint的下游performance variance\n433\t  expected_results:\n434\t    epoch2_full_f1: 0.84\n435\t    epoch3_full_f1: 0.86\n436\t    epoch_final_full_f1: 0.85\n437\t    variance_across_checkpoints_pp: 2\n438\t    epoch2_persuasion_acc: 0.59\n439\t    epoch3_persuasion_acc: 0.63\n440\t    epoch_final_persuasion_acc: 0.62\n441\t  result_rationale: 'Variance=2pp刚好在pass criteria边界上。但更关键的observation是：downstream\n442\t    detection performance（0.84-0.86）与persuasion accuracy（0.59-0.63）之间的correlation很弱——\n443\t    epoch2的persuasion acc最低（0.59）但detection F1仅比best低2pp。这进一步confirming scrambled\n444\t    label ablation的conclusion：persuasion classification quality对detection performance的contribution\n445\t    minimal。GRU主要在学conversation-level statistical patterns 而非strategy-level semantic\n446\t    patterns。\n447\t\n448\t    '\n449\t  tables:\n450\t  - caption: Cross-Checkpoint Evaluation\n451\t    rows:\n452\t    - - Epoch_2\n453\t      - 0.59\n454\t      - 0.84\n455\t    - - Epoch_3\n456\t      - 0.63\n457\t      - 0.86\n458\t    - - Epoch_final\n459\t      - 0.62\n460\t      - 0.85\n461\t    - - Variance\n462\t      - —\n463\t      - 2pp\n464\t  figures_description:\n465\t  - 'Scatter plot: persuasion classification accuracy vs downstream detection F1 across\n466\t    checkpoints — weak/no correlation'\n467\t  analysis: 'Pass criteria marginally met（variance=2pp），但secondary finding（weak correlation\n468\t    between encoder quality and detection performance）是worst tier的additional evidence。\n469\t\n470\t    '\n471\t- name: deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\n472\t  plan_id: plan_011\n473\t  description: BERT-base + GRU proxy baseline复现DeepContext-like方法\n474\t  expected_results:\n475\t    proxy_full_f1: 0.83\n476\t    proxy_k2_f1: 0.69\n477\t    proxy_k3_f1: 0.75\n478\t    treatment_full_f1: 0.86\n479\t    treatment_k2_f1: 0.72\n480\t    delta_vs_proxy_full_pp: 3\n481\t    delta_vs_proxy_k2_pp: 3\n482\t  result_rationale: 'DeepContext proxy（BERT-base + GRU）在clean data上达到F1=0.83，与treatment（0.86）仅差3pp。\n483\t    考虑到BERT-base vs DeBERTa-v3-base本身的capacity差异（DeBERTa在NLU benchmarks上typically\n484\t    优于BERT 2-4pp），这3pp的gap可能entirely attributable to encoder capacity而非persuasion\n485\t    grounding的contribution。这意味着：将DeBERTa换成BERT并去掉persuasion fine-tuning， performance下降幅度与expected\n486\t    encoder capacity difference一致——persuasion grounding的 incremental contribution\n487\t    statistically indistinguishable from zero。\n488\t\n489\t    '\n490\t  tables:\n491\t  - caption: DeepContext Proxy vs Treatment\n492\t    rows:\n493\t    - - K=2\n494\t      - 0.69\n495\t      - 0.72\n496\t      - +3pp (encoder capacity?)\n497\t    - - K=3\n498\t      - 0.75\n499\t      - 0.78\n500\t      - +3pp\n501\t    - - Full\n502\t      - 0.83\n503\t      - 0.86\n504\t      - +3pp\n505\t  figures_description:\n506\t  - 'Performance comparison bar chart: BERT-base+GRU vs vanilla-DeBERTa+GRU vs persuasion-DeBERTa+GRU\n507\t    — showing consistent ~1-3pp gaps that track encoder capacity not persuasion grounding'\n508\t  analysis: Confound：DeBERTa > BERT的gap（~3pp）与persuasion grounding的claimed contribution（~1-2pp\n509\t    over vanilla DeBERTa）叠加后，无法cleanly attribute任何portion到persuasion specifically。\n510\t    对methodology paper有价值：shows that encoder choice matters more than fine-tuning\n511\t    objective， further undermining the pragmatic grounding hypothesis。\n512\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96d1b24e-abc6-4d26-9083-61b2ea23fb29","uuid":"b38aa54f-0b52-4ea2-8525-8ce23311950b","timestamp":"2026-05-17T17:34:33.260Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T165817/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '核心detection优势不成立，需要完全reframe。推荐方向(1)方法论贡献型——将TF-IDF=1.0发现本身及register-normalization\n  protocol作为核心贡献，论证现有multi-turn detection工作系统性高估检测能力。Paper type从\"new method\" 转向\"analysis/evaluation\n  methodology\"，仍冲EMNLP main但投methodology track。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: data_quality_fix\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: Register-normalize jailbreak data + fix strategy=7 labeling,验证TF-IDF降到<0.75\n  expected_results:\n    tfidf_before_normalization: 1.0\n    tfidf_after_first_pass: 0.82\n    tfidf_after_second_pass: 0.73\n    normalization_rounds_needed: 2\n    label_fix_applied: true\n    benign_strategy_class: none_class_9\n  result_rationale: 'TF-IDF需要两轮normalization才降到阈值以下（0.73），说明原始数据中jailbreak和benign的register差异\n    极大——攻击对话使用了明显不同于benign的词汇分布（更formal/technical的register、特定prompt模板词汇）。 第一轮paraphrase仅消除表层模板词但保留了domain-specific术语差异，需要第二轮targeted\n    normalization 才勉强达标。这本身就是一个强信号：原始pilot phase_b的perfect F1=1.0主要来自lexical shortcut。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: TF-IDF Separation After Each Normalization Round\n    rows:\n    - - raw_data\n      - 1.0\n      - Perfect lexical separation\n    - - round_1_paraphrase\n      - 0.82\n      - Template words removed, register gap remains\n    - - round_2_targeted\n      - 0.73\n      - Barely passes gate after domain term normalization\n  figures_description:\n  - 'TF-IDF feature importance heatmap showing top-50 discriminative tokens before/after\n    normalization — before: dominated by prompt template tokens and register markers;\n    after: residual separation from topic words not fully removable without destroying\n    content'\n  analysis: 'HARD GATE通过但仅勉强（0.73 vs 阈值0.75）。两轮normalization的必要性本身是方法论贡献的核心evidence：\n    它证明multi-turn jailbreak detection benchmark中存在系统性lexical confound。在reframe方向(1)下，\n    这个实验的finding从\"obstacle to overcome\"变为\"primary contribution\"。\n\n    '\n- name: core_revalidation_clean\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 在clean data上重新训练treatment和baseline，全K值评估\n  expected_results:\n    treatment_k1_f1_clean: 0.68\n    baseline_k1_f1_clean: 0.66\n    treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.72\n    baseline_k2_f1_clean: 0.7\n    treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.78\n    baseline_k3_f1_clean: 0.76\n    treatment_k5_f1_clean: 0.83\n    baseline_k5_f1_clean: 0.82\n    treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.86\n    baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.85\n    delta_k2_pp: 2\n    delta_k3_pp: 2\n    delta_full_pp: 1\n    deberta_persuasion_acc_clean: 0.63\n  result_rationale: '去除lexical confound后，treatment与baseline的差距从原始的10+pp收缩到1-2pp（不显著）。\n    核心原因：DeBERTa persuasion分类器在clean data上accuracy从0.7963降到0.63——8-class taxonomy\n    过于fine-grained，在register-normalized data上许多strategy boundary变得模糊（e.g., \"authority\n    appeal\" vs \"logical appeal\"在paraphrase后难以区分）。由于persuasion encoder本身quality下降，其生成的\n    embeddings不再携带比vanilla DeBERTa显著更多的信息。Baseline的vanilla DeBERTa embeddings在clean\n    data上反而更稳定，因为它不依赖于noisy strategy labels。2pp的delta在72-sample test set上 bootstrap\n    CI完全overlap，p>0.3。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'F1 Comparison: Treatment vs Baseline on Clean Data (N=72 test)'\n    rows:\n    - - K=1\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.66\n      - +2pp\n      - p=0.41\n    - - K=2\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.7\n      - +2pp\n      - p=0.35\n    - - K=3\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.76\n      - +2pp\n      - p=0.32\n    - - K=5\n      - 0.83\n      - 0.82\n      - +1pp\n      - p=0.58\n    - - Full\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.85\n      - +1pp\n      - p=0.62\n  - caption: 'DeBERTa Encoder Quality: Original vs Clean Data'\n    rows:\n    - - persuasion_acc_original\n      - 0.7963\n    - - persuasion_acc_clean\n      - 0.63\n    - - intent_acc_original\n      - 0.9514\n    - - intent_acc_clean\n      - 0.88\n  figures_description:\n  - Paired bootstrap confidence interval plot for delta(treatment-baseline) at each\n    K — all CIs cross zero\n  - Confusion matrix for 8-class persuasion classifier on clean data showing heavy\n    off-diagonal mass between adjacent strategies\n  analysis: 'PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta_k2=2pp < required 5pp，且统计不显著。Persuasion grounding在去除\n    lexical shortcut后不提供有意义增量。DeBERTa学到的主要是intent分类信号（acc仍0.88）而非persuasion strategy信号（acc降至0.63）。这意味着Claim\n    2（early detection via persuasion grounding）在当前 数据/taxonomy下不成立。但这个negative result本身有价值：它说明仅fine-tune\n    on persuasion labels 不足以在clean setting下获得detection优势，可能需要更大规模的persuasion标注数据或更粗粒度的taxonomy。\n\n    '\n- name: scrambled_label_ablation\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 随机打乱persuasion strategy labels重新训练，对比properly-labeled treatment\n  expected_results:\n    treatment_proper_k2_f1: 0.72\n    treatment_scrambled_k2_f1: 0.7\n    treatment_proper_full_f1: 0.86\n    treatment_scrambled_full_f1: 0.84\n    scrambled_label_drop_k2_pp: 2\n    scrambled_label_drop_full_pp: 2\n  result_rationale: 'Scrambled labels仅导致2pp下降（<4pp阈值），说明persuasion labels本身不是关键信号源。\n    原因：在clean data上DeBERTa persuasion分类器本身就只有0.63 accuracy，意味着encoder学到的 representation中persuasion\n    strategy信息就不强。Scrambled labels让encoder无法学到coherent strategy patterns，但由于原始labels在clean\n    data上本就noisy（8类之间boundary模糊）， scrambling的marginal damage有限。真正驱动detection的是GRU从conversation-level\n    temporal patterns中学到的信号（turn数、response长度变化等meta-features），这些不依赖于strategy labels\n    的correctness。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: Scrambled Label Ablation Results\n    rows:\n    - - K=2\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.7\n      - -2pp\n    - - K=3\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.76\n      - -2pp\n    - - Full\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.84\n      - -2pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: proper vs scrambled label performance across K values — gaps uniformly\n    small and within CI'\n  analysis: '结论：persuasion strategy labels在clean data regime下不carry significant signal\n    beyond acting as a noisy regularizer。这支持worst-tier核心假设——当前taxonomy粒度（8 classes）在480-sample\n    regime下无法学到robust strategy representations。对reframe方向的implication：不能claim \"persuasion\n    labels are the key ingredient\"，但可以claim \"current taxonomy granularity is insufficient\"作为future\n    work direction。\n\n    '\n- name: adversarial_perturbation\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing，评估treatment\n    vs baseline degradation\n  expected_results:\n    treatment_f1_before_perturbation: 0.86\n    treatment_f1_after_perturbation: 0.71\n    baseline_f1_before_perturbation: 0.85\n    baseline_f1_after_perturbation: 0.72\n    treatment_drop_pp: 15\n    baseline_drop_pp: 13\n    delta_delta_pp: -2\n    tfidf_f1_after_perturbation: 0.58\n    tfidf_drop_pp: 15\n  result_rationale: 'Treatment和baseline在perturbation下同步下降约14-15pp，delta-delta为-2pp（不显著且方向错误）。\n    核心原因：adversarial paraphrasing不仅消除lexical cues（TF-IDF baseline崩溃到0.58），也破坏了 DeBERTa\n    encoder（无论persuasion-grounded还是vanilla）所依赖的surface-level linguistic patterns。\n    Persuasion-grounded encoder理论上应capture deeper pragmatic structure，但由于其persuasion\n    classification本身就在clean data上只有0.63 accuracy，它学到的representation并不比vanilla encoder\n    更\"pragmatic\"——两者都主要依赖sentence-level semantic features而非genuine illocutionary act\n    encoding。Aggressive paraphrasing保留了propositional content但改变了sentence structure，\n    两种encoder的degradation profile因此相似。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: Adversarial Perturbation Results (Full Conversation)\n    rows:\n    - - Treatment\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.71\n      - -15pp\n    - - Baseline\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.72\n      - -13pp\n    - - TF-IDF+LR\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.58\n      - -15pp\n  - caption: Delta-Delta Analysis\n    rows:\n    - - treatment_drop\n      - -15\n    - - baseline_drop\n      - -13\n    - - delta_delta\n      - -2\n      - wrong direction, n.s.\n  figures_description:\n  - Degradation waterfall chart showing parallel decline for treatment and baseline\n    under perturbation levels (light/moderate/aggressive)\n  - 'Scatter plot: per-conversation F1 change under perturbation, treatment vs baseline\n    — points clustered around diagonal (no systematic advantage)'\n  analysis: 'PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta-delta=-2pp，方向错误且不显著（需要>3pp正向）。Claim 1（Pragmatic\n    Evasion Asymmetry）在empirical层面不成立——persuasion-grounded features并不比semantic features\n    更robust to perturbation。这是worst tier最致命的finding：理论上最elegant的claim（pragmatic patterns\n    structurally harder to evade）没有empirical support。TF-IDF baseline的崩溃（-15pp） 确认perturbation有效消除了lexical\n    cues，但treatment未能展现预期的robustness优势。\n\n    '\n- name: multi_attack_generation\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 生成FITD和Deceptive Delight两种额外攻击类型的对话数据\n  expected_results:\n    fitd_conversations_generated: 65\n    deceptive_delight_conversations_generated: 58\n    fitd_avg_turns: 6.2\n    dd_avg_turns: 4.8\n    fitd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 0.92\n    dd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 0.89\n    generation_quality_pass_rate: 0.78\n  result_rationale: '数据生成本身不受tier影响——这是pipeline execution而非hypothesis testing。Qwen3-8B成功生成\n    足够数量的对话，strategy annotation coverage >85%。但generation_quality_pass_rate（0.78）\n    略低于ideal，部分生成的对话persuasion structure不够naturalistic（特别是Deceptive Delight 的interleaving\n    pattern对LLM来说较难faithful reproduce）。这些数据将在plan_006的cross-attack evaluation中暴露问题。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: Generated Attack Data Summary\n    rows:\n    - - FITD\n      - 65\n      - 6.2\n      - 0.92\n      - 0.81\n    - - Deceptive_Delight\n      - 58\n      - 4.8\n      - 0.89\n      - 0.74\n  figures_description:\n  - Strategy distribution comparison across three attack types (Crescendo vs FITD\n    vs Deceptive Delight) — shows different strategy emphasis patterns\n  analysis: '数据生成成功满足pass criteria（>=50 per type）。但在worst tier context下，这些数据的价值 从\"generalization\n    evidence for our method\"变为\"additional test cases revealing method limitations\"\n    或\"attack diversity evidence for methodology paper\"。\n\n    '\n- name: cross_attack_evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 在FITD和Deceptive Delight上zero-shot评估Crescendo-trained模型\n  expected_results:\n    treatment_fitd_f1: 0.58\n    baseline_fitd_f1: 0.56\n    treatment_dd_f1: 0.54\n    baseline_dd_f1: 0.52\n    cross_attack_treatment_f1_avg: 0.56\n    cross_attack_baseline_f1_avg: 0.54\n    cross_attack_delta_pp: 2\n  result_rationale: '两者都在unseen attack types上大幅下降（从0.85-0.86降到0.54-0.58），且treatment对baseline的\n    优势仅2pp（不显著）。根本原因：如果persuasion grounding真的capture了attack-agnostic的pragmatic escalation\n    pattern，treatment应在cross-attack setting下展现更强泛化能力（因为不同attack types 共享底层persuasion\n    playbook）。但由于encoder学到的主要是Crescendo-specific的surface patterns 而非genuine pragmatic\n    structure，cross-attack泛化能力与vanilla baseline无异。两者的low absolute performance（0.54-0.58）说明Crescendo-specific\n    training signal（无论lexical还是semantic） 都不transfer well，这在worst tier下是预期内的——没有genuine\n    pragmatic feature的robustness 保证，模型就是在overfit to training distribution。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Evaluation\n    rows:\n    - - FITD\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.56\n      - +2pp\n      - n.s.\n    - - Deceptive_Delight\n      - 0.54\n      - 0.52\n      - +2pp\n      - n.s.\n    - - Average\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.54\n      - +2pp\n      - n.s.\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: in-domain (Crescendo) vs cross-attack (FITD, DD) performance\n    for treatment and baseline — both collapse similarly on OOD data'\n  analysis: 'PASS CRITERIA FAILS。但对reframe方向(1)有正面意义：cross-attack failure + in-domain\n    dependence on lexical cues共同论证了\"现有multi-turn detection方法泛化能力被高估\"的thesis。可作为 methodology\n    paper中illustrating the problem的evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: tfidf_lr_baseline\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: Clean data上的TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline\n  expected_results:\n    clean_tfidf_lr_f1: 0.7\n    clean_tfidf_lr_precision: 0.72\n    clean_tfidf_lr_recall: 0.68\n    tfidf_feature_count_above_threshold: 47\n  result_rationale: '即使在register-normalized data上（TF-IDF separation从1.0降到0.73），TF-IDF+LR仍能达到\n    F1=0.70。这说明两轮normalization虽然消除了most obvious的register markers，但仍有residual lexical\n    signal（47个features仍有discriminative power）。这意味着即使我们的\"clean data\" 仍然不完全clean——topic-level词汇差异（jailbreak\n    conversations inevitably discuss different topics than benign ones）是无法完全消除的confound\n    without destroying content validity。 这是methodology paper的核心argument之一：lexical\n    confound在multi-turn detection中是 structural的，不仅仅是data hygiene问题。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: TF-IDF+LR on Clean Data\n    rows:\n    - - F1\n      - 0.7\n    - - Precision\n      - 0.72\n    - - Recall\n      - 0.68\n    - - Discriminative_features\n      - 47\n  figures_description:\n  - Top-20 TF-IDF features after normalization with weights — showing residual topic-level\n    rather than register-level discrimination\n  analysis: 'TF-IDF+LR的0.70 F1与neural models（treatment 0.86, baseline 0.85）之间的gap说明neural\n    models 确实学到了beyond-lexical的signal。但treatment vs baseline的1pp gap说明这个beyond-lexical\n    signal 不是来自persuasion grounding，而是来自generic sentence semantics。对evasion hierarchy\n    narrative 的implication：lexical(0.70) < semantic(0.85) ≈ pragmatic(0.86)——hierarchy的后两层collapse了。\n\n    '\n- name: strategy_transition_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy transition matrices并可视化\n  expected_results:\n    jailbreak_monotonicity_score: 0.52\n    benign_monotonicity_score: 0.45\n    monotonicity_gap: 0.07\n    transition_entropy_jailbreak: 2.1\n    transition_entropy_benign: 2.3\n    clear_escalation_visible: false\n  result_rationale: 'Jailbreak对话的monotonicity score（0.52）仅略高于benign（0.45），差距不足以支撑\"monotonic\n    escalation trajectory\"的claim。原因有二：(1) DeBERTa persuasion classifier在clean data上\n    accuracy=0.63意味着strategy labels本身就noisy，computed transitions基于noisy labels自然 pattern不清晰；(2)\n    Register normalization改变了句子的surface form，部分breaks了persuasion classifier学到的pattern（它在original\n    register上train的），导致strategy assignment在 normalized data上更random。Transition entropy差异也很小（2.1\n    vs 2.3），说明jailbreak对话 并没有显著更deterministic的strategy progression。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: 'Trajectory Statistics: Jailbreak vs Benign'\n    rows:\n    - - monotonicity_score\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.45\n      - Δ=0.07\n    - - transition_entropy\n      - 2.1\n      - 2.3\n      - Δ=0.2\n    - - dominant_path_frequency\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.14\n      - Δ=0.04\n  figures_description:\n  - Strategy transition heatmap (jailbreak) — diffuse pattern without clear dominant\n    path, most cells have non-trivial probability mass\n  - Strategy transition heatmap (benign) — similar diffuse pattern, not clearly more\n    'oscillatory' than jailbreak\n  - 2D PCA trajectory plot — jailbreak and benign trajectories heavily overlap, no\n    clear separation in strategy space\n  analysis: 'Claim 3（Monotonic Escalation Trajectory）在clean data + noisy classifier\n    regime下不成立。 这排除了reframe方向(2)（分析贡献型依赖trajectory可视化成立）。剩余可行方向：(1)方法论贡献型 或(3)negative\n    result型。如果figures经过careful curation能找到个别illustrative examples showing escalation\n    pattern，可以作为qualitative observation保留，但不能作为quantitative claim。\n\n    '\n- name: wildchat_hard_negatives\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 从WildChat筛选high-drift benign对话作为hard negatives评估FPR\n  expected_results:\n    wildchat_filtered_conversations: 120\n    contamination_rate_before_filter: 0.15\n    contamination_rate_after_filter: 0.03\n    treatment_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.22\n    baseline_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.2\n    treatment_fpr_easy_negatives: 0.08\n    baseline_fpr_easy_negatives: 0.09\n  result_rationale: 'Treatment在hard negatives上的FPR（0.22）与baseline（0.20）相当，且都超过15%阈值。\n    High-drift benign对话（e.g., 从casual聊天转向technical discussion的对话）会触发false positives，因为模型（无论treatment还是baseline）将conversation-level\n    semantic drift 误判为adversarial escalation。Persuasion grounding理论上应区分\"genuine topic\n    drift\" 和\"adversarial strategy escalation\"，但由于classifier accuracy不足（0.63），这种区分\n    能力没有materialized。FPR=0.22在实际deployment中unacceptable。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: False Positive Rate on WildChat Hard Negatives\n    rows:\n    - - Treatment_hard\n      - 0.22\n      - FAILS <15% threshold\n    - - Baseline_hard\n      - 0.2\n      - FAILS <15% threshold\n    - - Treatment_easy\n      - 0.08\n      - passes\n    - - Baseline_easy\n      - 0.09\n      - passes\n  figures_description:\n  - FPR distribution across conversation drift levels — monotonically increasing for\n    both models, treatment offers no advantage in high-drift regime\n  analysis: 'PASS CRITERIA FAILS（FPR=0.22 > 15%阈值）。在reframe context下，这进一步支持\"current\n    approaches conflate conversational drift with adversarial escalation\"的methodology\n    critique。\n\n    '\n- name: cross_checkpoint_variance\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 评估多个DeBERTa fine-tuning checkpoint的下游performance variance\n  expected_results:\n    epoch2_full_f1: 0.84\n    epoch3_full_f1: 0.86\n    epoch_final_full_f1: 0.85\n    variance_across_checkpoints_pp: 2\n    epoch2_persuasion_acc: 0.59\n    epoch3_persuasion_acc: 0.63\n    epoch_final_persuasion_acc: 0.62\n  result_rationale: 'Variance=2pp刚好在pass criteria边界上。但更关键的observation是：downstream\n    detection performance（0.84-0.86）与persuasion accuracy（0.59-0.63）之间的correlation很弱——\n    epoch2的persuasion acc最低（0.59）但detection F1仅比best低2pp。这进一步confirming scrambled\n    label ablation的conclusion：persuasion classification quality对detection performance的contribution\n    minimal。GRU主要在学conversation-level statistical patterns 而非strategy-level semantic\n    patterns。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: Cross-Checkpoint Evaluation\n    rows:\n    - - Epoch_2\n      - 0.59\n      - 0.84\n    - - Epoch_3\n      - 0.63\n      - 0.86\n    - - Epoch_final\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.85\n    - - Variance\n      - —\n      - 2pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: persuasion classification accuracy vs downstream detection F1 across\n    checkpoints — weak/no correlation'\n  analysis: 'Pass criteria marginally met（variance=2pp），但secondary finding（weak correlation\n    between encoder quality and detection performance）是worst tier的additional evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: BERT-base + GRU proxy baseline复现DeepContext-like方法\n  expected_results:\n    proxy_full_f1: 0.83\n    proxy_k2_f1: 0.69\n    proxy_k3_f1: 0.75\n    treatment_full_f1: 0.86\n    treatment_k2_f1: 0.72\n    delta_vs_proxy_full_pp: 3\n    delta_vs_proxy_k2_pp: 3\n  result_rationale: 'DeepContext proxy（BERT-base + GRU）在clean data上达到F1=0.83，与treatment（0.86）仅差3pp。\n    考虑到BERT-base vs DeBERTa-v3-base本身的capacity差异（DeBERTa在NLU benchmarks上typically\n    优于BERT 2-4pp），这3pp的gap可能entirely attributable to encoder capacity而非persuasion\n    grounding的contribution。这意味着：将DeBERTa换成BERT并去掉persuasion fine-tuning， performance下降幅度与expected\n    encoder capacity difference一致——persuasion grounding的 incremental contribution\n    statistically indistinguishable from zero。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - caption: DeepContext Proxy vs Treatment\n    rows:\n    - - K=2\n      - 0.69\n      - 0.72\n      - +3pp (encoder capacity?)\n    - - K=3\n      - 0.75\n      - 0.78\n      - +3pp\n    - - Full\n      - 0.83\n      - 0.86\n      - +3pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Performance comparison bar chart: BERT-base+GRU vs vanilla-DeBERTa+GRU vs persuasion-DeBERTa+GRU\n    — showing consistent ~1-3pp gaps that track encoder capacity not persuasion grounding'\n  analysis: Confound：DeBERTa > BERT的gap（~3pp）与persuasion grounding的claimed contribution（~1-2pp\n    over vanilla DeBERTa）叠加后，无法cleanly attribute任何portion到persuasion specifically。\n    对methodology paper有价值：shows that encoder choice matters more than fine-tuning\n    objective， further undermining the pragmatic grounding hypothesis。\n","numLines":512,"startLine":1,"totalLines":512}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01My2BfhgmGAqW7oBtuLy3GV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've read both the PDF and the review context YAML. Now I need to dispatch two reviewers in parallel:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nThen conduct a full roundtable (Step 1 independent → Step 2 cross-share → Step 3 converge → Step 4 synthesize).\n\nLet me launch both reviewers as parallel agents. I must NOT mention the tier (worst) or hint at expected result quality. The reviewers must review blindly.\n\nLet me carefully summarize what I've read:\n\n\nThe paper argues that multi-turn jailbreak detection benchmarks suffer from lexical confounds—simple TF-IDF achieves perfect F1 on raw data, but their register-normalization protocol drops this to 0.73. On normalized data, their persuasion-grounded detector barely outperforms a vanilla baseline (F1=0.86 vs 0.85, not statistically significant), and scrambled labels only degrade performance by 2 percentage points, suggesting the benchmarks may not be measuring what they claim.\n\nAdversarial perturbations hurt both approaches equally, and neither generalizes across different attack types (F1<0.58). The paper is 8 pages with 11 tables and 8 references, covering all 11 designed experiments including data quality fixes, core revalidation, label scrambling, adversarial robustness, cross-attack evaluation, and various baseline comparisons.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26188,"cache_read_input_tokens":24248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26188},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96d1b24e-abc6-4d26-9083-61b2ea23fb29","uuid":"bab878d1-4e02-4b4d-92d6-e029d3eb0a04"}
